 ", computing its total graph once."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"edb8139b-4149-48e2-8223-b63ef338aa1d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A fibration is a graph ",
 StyleBox["total", "TI"],
 ", the total graph, with a map ",
 StyleBox["proj", "TI"],
 " from its vertices to the vertices of a base graph. The fiber over a base \
vertex ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 " is the subgraph of ",
 StyleBox["total", "TI"],
 " on the vertices that ",
 StyleBox["proj", "TI"],
 " sends to ",
 StyleBox["p", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ac5cf2d4-f078-4341-b745-3d00c3703d0f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The base graph is not stored. ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraBaseGraph"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraBaseGraph", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c14d3069-2445-4ae3-bf03-4027098148cc"],
 " reconstructs it from the projection: two base vertices are adjacent iff \
some total edge projects onto them."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"4aa297dc-fd9c-46bc-b314-dba604da8a82"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraFibration"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraFibration", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d597fcd5-f925-483d-acfb-a3941bf11f7c"],
 " is inert. It holds the graph and the projection, and every function of the \
Infra Fiber Bundles guide reads them through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraTotalGraph"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraTotalGraph", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
